{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5C3powTZc4PGHn427m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `addMonths` in `dates.js`. The bug was that `setMonth` overflows: Jan 31 + 1 month became \"Feb 31\", which rolls over to Mar 3. That's why 31st-billed customers landed in the wrong month.\n\nThe function now moves to the 1st before changing the month, then clamps the day to the last day of the target month. Time of day is kept and the input date is not mutated.\n\nChecked by running it with Node:\n- Jan 15 + 1 → Feb 15 (matches the file's header comment)\n- Jan 31 + 1 → Feb 28 (2026), Feb 29 (2024)\n- Mar 31 − 1 → Feb 28\n- Jan 31 + 13 → Feb 28, 2027\n- Jan 31 13:45 + 1 → Feb 28 13:45\n- Jan 31 + 0 → Jan 31\n\nThis is a single-file change, and the repo isn't under git, so there's no diff to review. I didn't look at the billing code that calls `addMonths` or run any test suite, since I didn't find one.\n\nOne thing to confirm: customers billed on the 31st will now be billed on the 28th (or 29th in leap years) in short months. That's what the file's comment specifies, but if your billing policy is to roll to the 1st of the next month instead, the clamp logic needs to change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":582,"cache_read_input_tokens":24067,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":582},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49de8f66-a0da-479d-9731-51d0e58bb7d6","uuid":"ca7b00df-87f7-452a-8c04-04b11478afbc","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:30:02.131Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5C3aSGUpZyEBTd9iLB"}
